  "note": "Hindi spells English names by sound. Capital keys (E, I, AA…) are vowel letters at the start of a syllable; lowercase keys are a consonant plus a vowel sign (maa = मा). 'n+' is a half letter that joins the next one. English 't' and 'd' usually use ट and ड.",
